  "effect_registry_eligible": false,
  "reading": "The same Tribulus source supports a weak unadjusted island-continent flower-size contrast, a larger environment-adjusted contrast in the released author model, and a strong Galapagos-versus-other-island contrast. ID-level, continent-adjusted, and Galapagos-exclusion sensitivities are reported separately to show how much the headline island effect depends on repeated flower rows, source-pool composition, and Galapagos leverage.",
  "claim_boundary": "Tribulus is one widespread lineage with repeated flower measurements nested within source-defined IDs. Island/continent contrasts may show within-lineage floral divergence but do not create independent island colonisation pairs, do not measure effective pollinator dependency, and do not identify pollinator or geological-origin causation."
